# Pin line endings so a checkout is the same on every machine.
#
# Without this file, a clone made under Git for Windows' system default
# (core.autocrlf=true, set in <git install>/etc/gitconfig) rewrites every LF
# to CRLF on checkout -- and git still reports the tree as clean, so nothing
# warns you. docs/FORMAT.md then gets a \r inside its ```csv fence line, and
# test/core.test.js, which splits on '```csv\n', dies on item 12 with
# "TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'split')".
#
# Blobs in this repo are LF already, so this changes nothing for existing
# working trees; it only stops a fresh clone (or a Windows CI runner) from
# producing a red suite that no commit caused.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never rewrite bytes inside assets.
*.pdf binary
